n=null, bookDirection=null, companionDirection=null, remediationStepId=null), V2Step(id=u4-st-teach-present-говорить, kind=TEACH, title=Match we in the supplied speaking forms, body=The infinitive говори́ть names this entry. Match each supplied present form to its person: I: говорю́; you (one familiar person): говори́шь; he: говори́т; we: говори́м. When the check requests we, choose говори́м. Compare the written endings in these supplied forms; do not substitute the endings from the earlier reading example. First practise a different person from this same entry, then answer the requested person without using option position. These supplied choices do not demonstrate producing an unseen form., dominantAction=Continue, referenceIds=[ref-u35-attribution], itemIds=[], exampleIds=[ex-u4-present-говорить-мы], unavailableReason=null, bookDirection=null, companionDirection=null, remediationStepId=null), V2Step(id=u4-st-teach-present-видеть, kind=TEACH, title=Match he in the supplied seeing forms, body=The infinitive ви́деть names this entry. Match each supplied present form to its person: I: ви́жу; you (one familiar person): ви́дишь; he: ви́дит; we: ви́дим. When the check requests he, choose ви́дит. The infinitive alone does not tell you which supplied form to choose. Notice that the I form differs from the other forms here; learn the whole supplied forms. First practise a different person from this same entry, then answer the requested person without using option position. These supplied choices do not demonstrate producing an unseen form., dominantAction=Continue, referenceIds=[ref-u35-attribution], itemIds=[], exampleIds=[ex-u4-present-видеть-он], unavailableReason=null, bookDirection=null, companionDirection=null, remediationStepId=null), V2Step(id=u4-st-teach-present-писать, kind=TEACH, title=Match you (plural) in the supplied writing forms, body=The infinitive писа́ть names this entry. Match each supplied present form to its person: I: пишу́; you (one familiar person): пи́шешь; he: пи́шет; you (plural): пи́шете. When the check requests you (plural), choose пи́шете. The supplied present forms have a different written stem from the infinitive. Keep the written stress exactly as shown; do not append an ending to the whole infinitive. First practise a different person from this same entry, then answer the requested person without using option position. These supplied choices do not demonstrate producing an unseen form., dominantAction=Continue, referenceIds=[ref-u35-attribution], itemIds=[], exampleIds=[ex-u4-present-писать-вы], unavailableReason=null, bookDirection=null, companionDirection=null, remediationStepId=null), V2Step(id=u4-st-teach-present-идти, kind=TEACH, title=Match they in the supplied going forms, body=The infinitive идти́ names this entry. Match each supplied present form to its person: I: иду́; you (one familiar person): идёшь; he: идёт; they: иду́т. When the check requests they, choose иду́т. The supplied finite forms differ from the infinitive. Learn these whole forms; this card does not teach how to choose between motion verbs in context. First practise a different person from this same entry, then answer the requested person without using option position. These supplied choices do not demonstrate producing an unseen form., dominantAction=Continue, referenceIds=[ref-u35-attribution], itemIds=[], exampleIds=[ex-u4-present-идти-они], unavailableReason=null, bookDirection=null, companionDirection=null, remediationStepId=null), V2Step(id=u4-st-guided-present-говорить, kind=GUIDED, title=Practise I before the independent we check, body=Compare the supplied forms above. Choose I here; the independent check asks for a different person., dominantAction=Continue, referenceIds=[], itemIds=[u4-g-present-говорить-я], exampleIds=[], unavailableReason=null, bookDirection=null, companionDirection=null, remediationStepId=u4-st-rem-present), V2Step(id=u4-st-guided-present-видеть, kind=GUIDED, title=Practise I before the independent he check, body=Compare the supplied forms above. Choose I here; the independent check asks for a different person., dominantAction=Continue, referenceIds=[], itemIds=[u4-g-present-видеть-я], exampleIds=[], unavailableReason=null, bookDirection=null, companionDirection=null, remediationStepId=u4-st-rem-present), V2Step(id=u4-st-guided-present-писать, kind=GUIDED, title=Practise I before the independent you (plural) check, body=Compare the supplied forms above. Choose I here; the independent check asks for a different person., dominantAction=Continue, referenceIds=[], itemIds=[u4-g-present-писать-я], exampleIds=[], unavailableReason=null, bookDirection=null, companionDirection=null, remediationStepId=u4-st-rem-present), V2Step(id=u4-st-guided-present-идти, kind=GUIDED, title=Practise I before the independent they check, body=Compare the supplied forms above. Choose I here; the independent check asks for a different person., dominantAction=Continue, referenceIds=[], itemIds=[u4-g-present-идти-я], exampleIds=[], unavailableReason=null, bookDirection=null, companionDirection=null, remediationStepId=u4-st-rem-present), V2Step(id=u4-st-rem-present, kind=REMEDIATE, title=Remediation, body=The frozen page says: So, to form the present tense, you simply take the ''imperfective aspect'' of the verb and add the appropriate endings.

    These fields are copied from the admitted чита́ть row. Row glossed I: чита́ю. Row glossed you: чита́ешь. Row glossed he: чита́ет. 

    These fields are copied from the admitted чита́ть row. Row glossed we: чита́ем. Row glossed you (plural): чита́ете. Row glossed they: чита́ют. 

    де́лать — make. The admitted row records де́лаю for the row glossed I.

    These infinitives are copied from admitted rows. знать — know. рабо́тать — work. понима́ть — understand. слу́шать — listen. 

    These infinitives are copied from admitted rows. жить — live. говори́ть — to speak. ви́деть — see. смотре́ть — look. 

    These infinitives are copied from admitted rows. писа́ть — write. идти́ — go. 

    The infinitive говори́ть names this entry. Match each supplied present form to its person: I: говорю́; you (one familiar person): говори́шь; he: говори́т; we: говори́м. When the check requests we, choose говори́м. Compare the written endings in these supplied forms; do not substitute the endings from the earlier reading example. First practise a different person from this same entry, then answer the requested person without using option position. These supplied choices do not demonstrate producing an unseen form.

    The infinitive ви́деть names this entry. Match each supplied present form to its person: I: ви́жу; you (one familiar person): ви́дишь; he: ви́дит; we: ви́дим. When the check requests he, choose ви́дит. The infinitive alone does not tell you which supplied form to choose. Notice that the I form differs from the other forms here; learn the whole supplied forms. First practise a different person from this same entry, then answer the requested person without using option position. These supplied choices do not demonstrate producing an unseen form.

    The infinitive писа́ть names this entry. Match each supplied present form to its person: I: пишу́; you (one familiar person): пи́шешь; he: пи́шет; you (plural): пи́шете. When the check requests you (plural), choose пи́шете. The supplied present forms have a different written stem from the infinitive. Keep the written stress exactly as shown; do not append an ending to the whole infinitive. First practise a different person from this same entry, then answer the requested person without using option position. These supplied choices do not demonstrate producing an unseen form.

